+## The hub keys
+
+The hub keys screen (`apps/web/src/screens/keys`) draws `GET /api/keys` as it comes, in one panel, a key to a row: its id and note, the pools it opens (a reader key opens none, and says it opens the request log), when it was last used and the machine its last request was tagged with, and its requests and tokens of the last 7 days. A key never used says so and has no machine; a key whose requests reported no usage writes its tokens as `unreported`, and one with no requests as `none`. The scope narrows the list to one (or all), and the heads Last used and Requests order it (`keys.ts`: `narrowed`, `sorted`). The panel says the 7 days begin after the request log does when `logBegins` falls inside them (`shortWindow`). The screen takes its answer from whoever renders it; no route or endpoint exists yet.
